# Bandit Level 15 → Level 16

## Goal
The password for the next level can be retrieved by submitting the password of the current level to port 30001 on localhost using SSL/TLS encryption.

## Commands used
- whoami
- cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit15
- man openssl
- openssl s_client -connect localhost:30001 

## Explanation
- whoami this tells me who I am signed up as and it was bandit15
- cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit15 to display the password of the previous level since I will need it for this level
- man openssl this shows a manual for the openssl since I needed a better understanding of SSL encryption
- openssl is a tool for working with encryption and certificates
- s_client and essentially saying to start a tls client
- -connect localhost:30001 means connects to port 30001 on this machine

## Result
I received very output from the full code but once I inserted the previous password I got it correct and presented the password to the next level

## What I learned
the use case for openssl, s_client and using the command -connect when trying to access a seperate port.

